{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Diagrams in UML 2X, the Activity Diagram"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about UML diagrams."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Give detailed information related to UML and common related topics."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "develop"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to create, implement or build"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It says that software engineers use diagrams to represent the different processes that will help them develop computer programs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "of one's own"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that belongs to someone (depending on the subject)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm doing some examples of my own because instructors think that if we do them today, we will get to practice and pass the exam."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "timing "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "schedule, time control or measurement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Interaction diagrams focus more on the way objects are interacting with one another, it includes sequences and timing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deployment "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "distribution, placement or dissemination"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They don't take time into account, but focus more on composite structure, deployment, and packages."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "classmate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who takes classes with you"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was talking to other classmates, but they said they didn't know. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "phase, period or step"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After all, modeling is one of the first stages in software development."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about diagrams in UML"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose four diagrams"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a chart to explain each diagram in UML "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use first conditional with continuous sentences and time expressions in your explanation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Show your chart to your instructor. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about diagrams in UML. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I understand the way of those diagrams work in UML.. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain how some diagrams work in UML"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use first conditional with continuous sentences and time expressions in my explanation."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Continuous vs. Past Continuous "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use continuous tenses to refer to actions that are/were taking place or in development."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">present continuous </span>to talk about actions that are happening at the same moment of speaking. </br></br>  To make affirmative sentences, you can use the following structure: </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <b>verb to be (am/is/are) +verb (ing form)</b> + complement.</div></br></br>  Example: </br> <i> I <span class=\"strong\">am using </span>this modeling approach right now</i>. </br></br>  Note: You can also use contractions in this tense: </br></br>  Example: </br><i>  She<span class=\"strong\">'s having </span>problems with her keyboard.</i> </br></br>   We use <strong>past continuous</strong> to make a reference to actions that occurred during a period of time in the past. </br></br> To make affirmative sentences you can follow this structure: </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <b>verb to be in past (was/were) + verb (ing form)</b> + complement.</div></br></br> Example: </br><i>  Janet <span class=\"strong\">was working </span>on the program yesterday. </br> We <span class=\"strong\">were talking </span>to our boss about the advantages of structure diagrams.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let's see, I was reading about diagrams, it says that software engineers use diagrams to represent the different processes that will help them develop computer programs. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Finally, we have structure diagrams. We were reviewing them in our last class, "}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, I'm doing some examples of my own, because instructors think that if we do them today, we will get to practice and pass the exam."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "First Conditional with Continuous Sentences and Time Expressions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">first conditional </span>to talk an action that may have an impact in the future. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">first conditional </span>contains two clauses, the first one is the condition, and the second one is the result of the condition.</br></br>  The \u201c<span class=\"strong\">if</span>\u201d clause <span class=\"strong\">(condition) </span>goes in <b>simple present</b> or <b>present continuous</b>, while the second clause <span class=\"strong\">(result) </span>goes in <b>future simple</b>. </br></br> You can use time expressions to show that the action is happening at a specific moment. Some time expressions for continuous tenses include <i>now, right now, at this moment, as we speak</i>, and <i>nowadays</i>, etc. </br></br>  Follow this structure to build a sentence in the first conditional: </br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, I'm doing some examples of my own, because instructors think that if we do them today, we will get to practice and pass the exam. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we have a great modeling structure right now, creating software is not going to be as hard in the future."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we develop software using these diagrams now, we will see trends in the future as well."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If + present simple + , \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"+ future simple.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: </br></br>  <i>If <strong>you use</strong> UML now, you <strong>will develop </strong>software faster. </br> If <strong>you're using</strong> UML now, you <strong>will develop</strong> software faster. </i></br></br>  When you use the <i>present continuous</i>, you refer to current actions or arrangements. </br></br> Example: </br> <i> If the interaction diagram<strong> is not showing</strong> how objects interact at this moment, we will have to create a new one! </i></br><br>  Note that when you write the result before the condition, the comma is not necessary between the two clauses. </br></br> Example: </br> <i>You <strong>will develop</strong> software faster if you use diagrams<strong> right now</strong></i>."}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Tyra</strong>: Hey Brittany, we need to review some concepts for tomorrow, we have a test about diagrams in UML! </br>\n<strong>Brittany</strong>: I know! Let's see, I was reading about diagrams, it says that software engineers use diagrams to represent the different processes that will help them develop computer programs, and organize the set of instructions they are following in programming stages. Since UML refers to object-oriented modeling, we need to focus on the different options we have when developing software. </br>\n<strong>Tyra</strong>: Yes, some of the most important are behavior, interaction, and structure diagrams. Right? </br>"}, {"time": "37000", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Brittany</strong>: Yes. Behavior diagrams show activities, states, and cases. If we develop software using these diagrams now, we will see trends in the future as well. </br>\n<strong>Tyra</strong>: Okay, wait a minute, I was writing what you said. So, I see that interaction diagrams focus more on the way objects are interacting with one another, it includes sequences and timing. </br>\n<strong>Brittany</strong>: Correct. Finally, we have structure diagrams. We were reviewing them in our last class, they don't take time into account but focus more on composite structure, packages, and deployment diagrams, which show the execution architecture of the systems. </br>\n<strong>Tyra</strong>: Okay, so those are the most important ones, but I'm thinking about the test; do you think we will have to give an example of each? </br>"}, {"time": "90000", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Brittany</strong>: I was talking to other classmates, but they said they didn't know. However, I'm doing some examples of my own, because instructors think that if we do them today, we will get to practice and pass the exam. </br>\n<strong>Tyra</strong>: I know! After all, modeling is one of the first stages in software development. If we have a great modeling structure right now, creating software is not going to be as hard in the future. Why don't we create different diagrams based on the most important ones, in case we have to do that during the exam? </br>\n<strong>Brittany</strong>: Good idea!"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n4le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le02ob03re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 9, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give general information rela